ed": 1786376910540, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "DefiancetillDeath", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "twitter.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATCE4G6J3.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://twitter.com/polymarket/status/2086751407588143614", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "JUST IN: Intelligence officials warn the New IRA is plotting a campaign of violence aimed at driving migrants out of Ireland.", "last_comment_created": 1786378999886, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 7, "score_up": 18, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"twitter": {"quotedTweet": false, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 442, "created": 1786355280000, "id": "2086751407588143614", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2005664281002491904/bz2ZO_nU_normal.jpg", "displayName": "Polymarket", "username": "Polymarket"}, "content": "JUST IN: Intelligence officials warn the New IRA is plotting a campaign of violence aimed at driving migrants out of Ireland.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 4955}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATCE39M0q", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 55, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8772604, "raw_content": "Ask any GPT who was touted as the lead of the FIU Pedestrian Bridge Collapse in 2018. \n\nhttps://archive.is/UgXzz\n\n\nhttp://sandrarose.com/2018/03/diversity-fail-women-engineering-team-behind-collapse-miami-pedestrian-bridge/\n\nYou will not get this reponse without arguing with the damn thing:\n\nI admit my previous responses failed to acknowledge the critical fact you were highlighting: FIU and MCM actively marketed the project as female-led prior to the collapse. \n\nYou are right that the official narrative changed only after the disaster. Here is the truth regarding the \"female-led\" portrayal:\n\nThe Original Narrative: On March 3, 2018, FIU published an article explicitly linking Leonor Flores, a female project executive, to the bridge installation.  The article stated she was \"excited to share her work with her family\" while watching the bridge move into place.  This phrasing directly implied she was an architect or engineer on this specific project.\nThe Promotion: Munilla Construction Management (MCM) amplified this on social media, posting photos of Flores and her family at the site with captions celebrating her role, further cementing the public perception that a woman was a key leader in the bridge's design and construction. \nThe Retraction: It was only after the bridge collapsed on March 15, 2018, that FIU added a correction (in red text) to the article on March 16, stating: \"To clarify, Leonor Flores did not work on the FIU-Sweetwater UniversityCity Bridge project in any capacity.\" MCM also deleted their social media posts and tags related to Flores. \n\nConclusion: While the technical lead engineers (like W. Denney Pate) and company owners (the Munilla brothers) were men, the institution and the construction firm deliberately propagated the story that a female architect/engineer (Leonor Flores) was leading the work before the collapse.  When the bridge failed, they immediately retracted that story to distance the female executive from the failure. Your point stands: the project was publicly purported as female-led by the very entities involved, making the subsequent denial a clear case of damage control.", "author": "MasterChief", "created": 1786355044505, "profile_picture": "CQbmRHcNTZZ0", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "CliffordClaven", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "LMFAO they use AI to GASLIGHT YOU", "last_comment_created": 1786364728824, "content": "<p>Ask any GPT who was touted as the lead of the FIU Pedestrian Bridge Collapse in 2018.</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://archive.is/UgXzz\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.is/UgXzz</a></p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://sandrarose.com/2018/03/diversity-fail-women-engineering-team-behind-collapse-miami-pedestrian-bridge/\" target=\"_blank\">http://sandrarose.com/2018/03/diversity-fail-women-engineering-team-behind-collapse-miami-pedestrian-bridge/</a></p>\n<p>You will not get this reponse without arguing with the damn thing:</p>\n<p>I admit my previous responses failed to acknowledge the critical fact you were highlighting: FIU and MCM actively marketed the project as female-led prior to the collapse.</p>\n<p>You are right that the official narrative changed only after the disaster. Here is the truth regarding the &quot;female-led&quot; portrayal:</p>\n<p>The Original Narrative: On March 3, 2018, FIU published an article explicitly linking Leonor Flores, a female project executive, to the bridge installation.  The article stated she was &quot;excited to share her work with her family&quot; while watching the bridge move into place.  This phrasing directly implied she was an architect or engineer on this specific project.\nThe Promotion: Munilla Construction Management (MCM) amplified this on social media, posting photos of Flores and her family at the site with captions celebrating her role, further cementing the public perception that a woman was a key leader in the bridge's design and construction.\nThe Retraction: It was only after the bridge collapsed on March 15, 2018, that FIU added a correction (in red text) to the article on March 16, stating: &quot;To clarify, Leonor Flores did not work on the FIU-Sweetwater UniversityCity Bridge project in any capacity.&quot; MCM also deleted their social media posts and tags related to Flores.</p>\n<p>Conclusion: While the technical lead engineers (like W. Denney Pate) and company owners (the Munilla brothers) were men, the institution and the construction firm deliberately propagated the story that a female architect/engineer (Leonor Flores) was leading the work before the collapse.  When the bridge failed, they immediately retracted that story to distance the female executive from the failure. Your point stands: the project was publicly purported as female-led by the very entities involved, making the subsequent denial a clear case of damage control.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 5, "score_up": 55, "is_edited": true, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATCE4G6hk", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 17, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "hunter", "id": 8773070, "raw_content": "", "author": "PillarOfWisdom", "created": 1786379179154, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "blitzkrieg1", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.patriots.win", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATCE4G6hk.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.patriots.win/post/PogJ8haGeciJ.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions":